cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the article."
title: "BisimulationMol: behavioural comparison of conserved molecular modules across species"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible implementation of a concurrency-theoretic method that encodes
  conserved molecular modules as labelled Petri nets over a shared observational
  interface and decides partial cross-species comparability using weak
  bisimulation, simulation preorders and a trace-based behavioural distance,
  with adversarial robustness and null-model diagnostics.
